<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian Stocks to Watch Today - July 7.</title>
<headline>Australian Stocks to Watch Today - July 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some Australian stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>* ANZ Banking Group Ltd A$9.87 (+0.12)</p>
<p>* Westpac Banking Corp A$7.91 (-0.03)</p>
<p>HSBC Holdings Plc's group chairman Sir William Purves said the banking group did not have an acquisition &quot;shopping list&quot; involving Australian banks. &quot;We don't have a shopping list and I don't have Australia on any list at all at this time,&quot; Purves told Channel Nine Business Sunday television programme. He had been asked if the bank's expansion plans included takeovers or mergers.</p>
<p>* Energy Equity Ltd A$1.55 (-0.04)</p>
<p>* Novus Petroluem A$4.47 (-0.03)</p>
<p>Energy Equity Corp Ltd said on Monday production testing at its Singa-1 exploration well has resulted in significant gas flows and confirmed a major discovery.</p>
<p>* Bass Strait Oil Trust</p>
<p>Bass Strait Oil Trust to list.</p>
<p>* Greenfields Coal Ltd A$0.14 (unch)</p>
<p>Greenfields Coal Co Ltd, which is developing a coal recovery plant in the United States, said on Friday that a share-swap takeover offer by Mineral Resources Corp (MRC) of Canada was not welcome.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
